<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pakuan Pajajaran</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pakuan Pajajaran was the capital of the Sunda Kingdom in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, on the site of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bogor">Bogor</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-baduga-maharaja">Sri Baduga Maharaja</a> ruled from it after uniting <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sunda-strait">Sunda</a> and Galuh in 1482 and strengthened it with a moat, as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batutulis-inscription">Batutulis inscription</a> records. The Portuguese visited the kingdom in the 1520s. The Banten Sultanate captured and destroyed the city in 1579, ending the kingdom.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pakuan-pajajaran.jpg" alt="Pakuan Pajajaran" width="320" height="290" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hadiyana · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pakuanpajajaran.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
